  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-3,7]?$\n\n- ${-3,-5,1,2,6}$\n- ${-3,0,3,7,8}$\n- ${-3,-2,1,3,4,7}$",
  "worked_solution": "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<\u2026<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},\u2026,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[-3,7]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=7.$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-3,7]$ since $8$ does not belong to $[-3,7].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[-3,7].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
